      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 0,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "Quasi-dense stereo: SEED AND GROW. StereoSGBM (bottom row) searches a disparity range at every pixel independently and needs that range set correctly; cv2.stereo.QuasiDenseStereo tracks a few hundred goodFeaturesToTrack seeds with Lucas-Kanade and then grows each match into its neighbours while the correlation and the local disparity gradient hold - no disparity range to get wrong, and on this pair ~700 seeds turn into ~360000 matches. It answers on MORE of the frame than SGBM here and agrees with it where both answer (see the difference map), but it answers only where there is texture to propagate through. Two traps this workflow makes visible. First, the class's own getDisparity() is the UNSIGNED EUCLIDEAN displacement sqrt(dx^2+dy^2), not the signed horizontal disparity every other stereo node emits - the node returns both, and they differ wherever a match drifted vertically. Second, a texture-less pair (the last row) gives goodFeaturesToTrack nothing to track and cv2 ASSERTS inside Lucas-Kanade; the node catches that and reports found=false with empty arrays."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
